---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import Section from '../components/Section.astro';
---
<BaseLayout
  title="Acceptable Use Policy | ZoneOfWar"
  description="Rules of engagement and acceptable-use requirements for ZoneOfWar drone cyber range missions and labs."
>
  <Section containerClass="max-w-3xl">
    <p class="font-mono text-xs uppercase tracking-wide text-accent">Legal</p>
    <h1 class="mt-3 text-3xl font-bold text-text sm:text-4xl">Acceptable Use Policy</h1>
    <p class="mt-2 text-sm text-text-faint">Last updated: 18 August 2026</p>

    <div class="prose-zow mt-8">
      <p>
        This Acceptable Use Policy sets the rules of engagement for every ZoneOfWar mission, lab and exercise. It
        applies to all users, including individual accounts, team members and instructor-led cohorts. Acceptance is
        required, with version and timestamp recorded, before any account can enter a hands-on lab.
      </p>

      <h2>1. Authorized environments only</h2>
      <p>
        All offensive and defensive techniques practiced on ZoneOfWar must stay inside the isolated environments we
        provide. You may never apply techniques learned on the platform to real drones, networks, or systems that you
        do not own and are not explicitly authorized in writing to test.
      </p>

      <h2>2. No real-world interference</h2>
      <p>
        You agree not to use ZoneOfWar, or knowledge gained from it, to jam, spoof, or otherwise interfere with real
        aircraft, spectrum, navigation systems or public communications. Any advanced physical RF or hardware-in-the-loop
        work is only available in separately controlled, legally compliant environments with explicit approval.
      </p>

      <h2>3. No unauthorized access</h2>
      <p>
        You agree not to attempt to access other users' or organizations' data, mission environments or accounts
        without authorization, and not to attempt to bypass platform isolation, monitoring or safety controls.
      </p>

      <h2>4. Respect scoring and evidence integrity</h2>
      <p>
        Do not attempt to manipulate scoring systems, falsify evidence, or misrepresent completed missions,
        certificates or skill records.
      </p>

      <h2>5. Team and instructor-led exercises</h2>
      <p>
        Red vs Blue and other multi-user exercises must stay within the mission's stated rules of engagement.
        Instructors are responsible for briefing participants and may pause, reset or end an exercise at any time.
      </p>

      <h2>6. Restricted and advanced content</h2>
      <p>
        Some advanced or hardware-enabled labs require additional terms, organization approval, or manual vetting
        before access is granted, and may be subject to export-control or sanctions screening.
      </p>

      <h2>7. Reporting concerns</h2>
      <p>
        If you believe another user has violated this policy, or you discover a security issue, report it to
        <a href="mailto:security@zoneofwar.com">security@zoneofwar.com</a>. See our
        <a href="/company/responsible-use">Responsible Use principles</a> for the broader context behind these rules.
      </p>

      <h2>8. Enforcement</h2>
      <p>
        Violating this policy may result in suspension or termination of your account and, where required by law,
        referral to relevant authorities.
      </p>
    </div>
  </Section>
</BaseLayout>
